libxtc (1.40.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(blocking): new public xtc_blocking_run_off_loop(fn, arg,
    out_result) -- offload a blocking call to the pool from a plain OS
    thread that is NOT a libxtc fiber, blocking the caller on the
    completion pipe with a real read(2) instead of parking a fiber, so
    fn runs on a pool worker rather than inline on the caller.  Answers
    the PostgreSQL pooled-carrier blocking-fsync consult (2026-08-28):
    a bare carrier pthread previously ran every offload inline because
    xtc_blocking_run needs a fiber and xtc_blocking_submit gives no
    result.  Documented honest contract (still synchronous from the
    caller's view, does not shorten a lock held across the call; a
    building block for group-commit offload, not a substitute for making
    sessions fibers) in xtc_blocking(3) and the header.  Rejected
    (XTC_E_INVAL) from a fiber.  Test: m9 blocking/off_loop.

