libxtc (1.39.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * feat(loop): new public xtc_loop_wake(xtc_loop_t *) -- a lost-wake-free
    loop-handle nudge, the loop-level companion to xtc_proc_wake().  A
    consumer that schedules by loop handle (e.g. an xtc_exec carrier
    scheduler like the PostgreSQL pooled-protocol carriers) can now wake
    a specific loop's poller from any OS thread after making a condition
    true for a task parked on it -- without reaching into the opaque
    xtc_loop_t for loop->io.  Closes the usability gap behind the
    PostgreSQL cross-loop wake-miss report (2026-08-28): the reported
    stalls are the documented producer-must-nudge contract (raw foreign
    fd readiness races the loop park/re-arm window); xtc_loop_wake is the
    sanctioned nudge.  Documented in xtc_loop(3) and the header;
    foreign-OS-thread wake test added (m5 cross_wake Cw5).

