libxtc (1.35.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * fix(rexis): flush the reply before parking in the connection loop.
    An un-pipelined request stalled ~1.00s because the loop parked
    waiting for the next inbound event (1s re-check timeout) before
    flushing the reply it had just produced.  Measured after the fix
    (EC2 aarch64): single-request SET/GET/PING p50 18us, p99 24us (was
    1,000,000us); redis-benchmark ~108-128k req/s.
  * fix(kaka): bound broker memory under a producer flood.  The
    partition log retained every appended record in RAM for the life of
    the partition -- even records already rolled to durable on-disk
    segments -- so RSS grew ~linearly with total messages (a 40M-message
    soak reached ~5.25 GB, contradicting the README's "bounded memory"
    claim).  Now records in closed segments are evicted from RAM and
    cold reads fall back to the segment files, bounding resident memory
    to ~2 segments; new test_partition/bounded_memory proves it (20,000
    appends -> RAM peak ~1,300 records, evicted reads still correct).

  Both bugs were found by multi-hour p99/p999 example load testing on
  EC2 (x86_64 + aarch64).  Library core unchanged from 1.35.1; these are
  example fixes.

