libxtc (1.35.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * fix(loop): initialize a task's fields BEFORE publishing it to the
    work-stealing deque.  xtc_deque_push() makes the task visible to
    thieves on other loops, and a thief writes stolen->q_next; writing
    t->q_next after the push raced the thief on the same field (both
    store NULL, benign in value, but a genuine publish-before-init
    ordering bug ThreadSanitizer flags).  Set it first, then publish.
  * fix(exec): make the per-worker NUMA steal hint (exec->loop_node) a
    relaxed atomic.  Each worker wrote its own slot at startup while
    thieves read other slots on the steal path -- non-atomic concurrent
    access (UB, though only a suboptimal steal-placement hint).
  * harden(osproc): close inherited file descriptors before execvp()
    (CWE-403).  The exec path let a child inherit the parent's
    event-loop/epoll/io_uring fds, sockets, TLS connections, and any
    embedder fd; now closes every fd >= 3 except the control fd via
    close_range(2) (fallback: bounded close() loop), async-signal-safe.
  * harden(slab): overflow guards in xtc_slab_create().  Reject an
    obj_size large enough that obj_size + redzones + align rounding
    wraps slot_size (which would hand out overlapping slots); rewrite
    the shared-memory size check as a subtraction that cannot wrap.
  * test: skip the deliberate-fault probes (stack-guard, pkey, proc
    fault-containment, scope) under gcc ThreadSanitizer too (they
    already skipped under clang TSan and ASan); add a full-suite TSan
    recipe (setarch -R + detect_deadlocks=0 + .github/tsan.supp
    cataloguing the documented-benign executor/steal hint races).
    Fix the ASan full make check (stack-guard test) so it runs clean.
  * test(exec): unit-cover the proportional-share class accessors
    (create validation + read-back + NULL-returns-0), previously only
    reached via the DST/PBT tests.
  * docs: correct the left-right lock attribution to Jon Gjengset
    (github.com/jonhoo/left-right); mark PLAN.md a historical design
    document; drop stale/agent phrasing from README and M_LIBC_MATRIX.

  Validated at scale on EC2 x86_64 (c7i) and aarch64 (c7g): gcc, clang,
  ASan, UBSan clean on both; ThreadSanitizer zero data races; a
  900k-seed DST swarm (up to 500k/arch across partition + latency +
  buggify + machine-death + torn-write) with zero invariant violations.

