libxtc (1.28.1-1) unstable; urgency=high

  * fix: xtc_task_waker() now names the loop a task is CURRENTLY
    runnable on, not the loop it was spawned on.  A migratable
    (xtc_proc_opts_t.migratable=1) proc's waker previously kept naming
    its stale spawn-time loop after being work-stolen; a wake
    (xtc_proc_wake / xtc_waker_wake) then targeted the wrong loop.
    Usually self-healing (the misdirected task sits on the wrong
    loop's stealable deque and a later steal picks it back up), so the
    symptom was intermittent -- but a PERMANENT strand under fast
    shutdown, when every worker can observe the stop signal and exit
    before anyone steals the entry back.  Silent by design
    (xtc_proc_wake treats a cross-thread wake as fire-and-forget).
    Confirmed and adversarially proven with a regression test.  No API
    change; migratable/work-stealing consumers should update.

