libxtc (1.27.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * exec: xtc_exec_set_eager_rebalance (opt-in, OFF by default) -- makes
    migratable procs actually rebalance under a realistic load.  By
    default a loop steals only when FULLY idle, so under a load where
    every loop owns parked fibers (server backends parked on sockets
    while a peer has a runnable query) no steal ever happens and
    migratable=1 is inert.  Eager rebalance lets a run-queue-empty (but
    fd/timer-parked) loop steal before blocking, and nudges an idle
    peer when migratable work is produced.  Only migratable tasks move;
    pinned work is unaffected.  Unblocks the PostgreSQL work-stealing
    idle-reclamation case.
  * No breaking API changes (additive, default off).

