libxtc (1.25.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * proc: xtc_proc_opts_t.migratable (opt-in, default 0 = pinned,
    unchanged).  A migratable proc's coroutine is work-stealable: on a
    multi-loop executor an idle loop may steal a parked/scheduled proc
    (never mid-instruction) to rebalance runnable work.  The proc's
    identity (pid/xtc_self), supervision (links/monitors/DOWN), recovery
    frame, and mailbox all survive the carrier change -- proven under
    the deterministic simulator (test_sim_migratable: forced
    cross-loop steals with identity + DOWN asserted, byte-identical
    replay).  Unblocks work-stealing for supervised backend procs.
  * inc: internal __-prefixed declarations moved out of the installed
    public headers into *_int.h internal headers (only a public macro's
    backing symbol may remain, e.g. the proc recovery seam); a new
    [C7] gate enforces it.
  * abi: the shared library now exports exactly the public surface --
    xtc_* plus only the macro-backed recovery symbols; the whole __os_*
    layer and every other __xtc_* internal are hidden from the .so ABI
    (previously a broad __xtc_* glob leaked ~80 internals).  A new [C8]
    gate keeps the version script from drifting.
  * No breaking API changes (all additions / internal-only).

