      input SCRAM channel binding needs).
  * OS: dedicated errno abstraction (M1.5).  __os_errno_map(errno) ->
    XTC_E_* as the one canonical translation, with an embedder hook
    (__os_errno_set_hook / _get_hook) for consumers that shim the
    underlying syscalls; consolidates two duplicated per-file tables.
  * No breaking API changes (all additions).

 -- Greg Burd <greg@burd.me>  Mon, 20 Jul 2026 13:51:27 -0400

libxtc (1.23.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix (scheduler): drain due timers under a busy run queue.  A loop
    that never emptied its run queue (a fiber that keeps rescheduling
    -- a busy xtc_yield / XTC_TASK_RESCHED spin) starved timer-based
    wakeups indefinitely: xtc_proc_sleep, a recv timeout, or any
    deadline would never fire, because the loop only expired timers
    once the run queue drained.  The scheduler now drains due timers on
    the IO-fairness quantum under load too (symmetric with the existing
    I/O-completion poll).  Surfaced by a cross-loop btree benchmark;
    the buggify "fire late" logic and DST replay-determinism are
    preserved.
  * No API change.

