libxtc (1.22.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: closed a pre-existing cross-thread data race on the receive
    waker (recv_waker).  __mbox_deliver read recv_waker after unlocking
    mbox_lock -- to fire the wake outside the lock -- while the woken
    receiver re-armed recv_waker under its own lock on its next recv
    cycle.  Benign in value (recv_waker is always the proc's own fixed
    task/loop) but a real C11 data race on every cross-thread xtc_send,
    surfaced under ThreadSanitizer by a new proc-table stress test.
    The wake now copies the waker out under the lock and fires from the
    copy (still outside the lock, no reentrancy).
  * Testing: the proc-table stress test is now part of the tsan-fibers
    CI gate, making the fix a permanent regression guard; added
    fault-injection coverage for the xtc_svr_reply OOM path (both
    reply branches).
  * No API change.

