libxtc (1.6.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New public API: xtc_alrlock_create / xtc_alrlock_create_ex -- the
    fiber-aware left-right lock.  Reads are wait-free and never block; the
    one place a left-right lock waits is the writer's publish (for
    in-flight readers to advance past the version swap), and when the
    writer runs inside a fiber that wait now yields the FIBER back to its
    loop instead of spinning the OS thread, so reader fibers advance and
    the loop keeps serving other work.  The behavior is automatic in
    xtc_lrlock_publish (purely additive, gated on fiber context, so a
    writer on a plain OS thread is byte-identical to before); the
    xtc_alrlock_* names let a fiber-based consumer express the intent.
    See xtc_lrlock(3).
  * Documentation site expanded substantially (no library behavior
    change): an in-site API reference rendered and colorized from the man
    pages and grouped by layer (with a "Foundational basics" group for the
    POSIX/libc rough-edge smoothers -- alloc/clock/sleep/atomics, stats,
    log, strerror, cfg, version); a Testing section (DST, property-based
    testing via Hegel, sanitizers, cross-platform verification); a
    Benchmarking section (honest methodology, warts and all); a
    resource-limits guide chapter and a Limits reference page; per-example
    "how libxtc concepts are applied" sections with diagrams; two new
    philosophy essays ("Let it crash" and "Message passing and the
    compromise"); mermaid diagrams throughout with a CI validation gate;
    and a documentation link checker.  The docs build and deploy to
    GitHub Pages and Codeberg Pages.
  * Doc-accuracy pass: removed stale PLAN.md / M0_CLAIMS.md / M16 / L5-pg
    references; the ARCHITECTURE doc gate now checks layers L0-L4.

