libxtc (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First stable release.  The public API surface is stable; semver
    applies from here (see docs/abi-stability.md).
  * Deterministic Simulation Testing (DST) at FoundationDB-class depth:
    ALL concurrency primitives run under a seeded single-thread
    simulator with bit-identical replay -- scheduler/work-stealing,
    every lock (amutex, arwlock, lockmgr, lwlock, lrlock), sem/gate/
    barrier/notify, channels (mpsc/mpmc/watch/broadcast), gen_server,
    registry, RCU, mctx/slab/stats/pdict -- plus network-partition,
    machine-death, WAL crash-recovery, torn/corrupt-write injection,
    11 Buggify sites, per-step invariant checks, and a 100k-seed
    nightly swarm in CI.  29 replay-verified sim tests; the effort
    caught ~7 real concurrency bugs.
  * Native preemption facility: cooperative-assisted (Phase 1,
    supported) plus true signal-context involuntary preemption on
    x86-64 and aarch64 (opt-in), with library-wide preemption-safe
    locks.
  * sqlxtc STEAL milestone: torn-tail WAL checksum, value-staging STEAL
    of oversized uncommitted transactions, and physiological
    per-non-split-leaf page logging for exact in-place torn recovery.
    NO-STEAL + NO-FORCE remains the correct, settled default.
  * PostgreSQL adapter (M16): the runtime seam is proven -- threaded
    PostgreSQL client backends run as xtc_proc fibers on the xtc
    scheduler (out-of-tree; see docs/M16_PG_ADAPTER.md).
  * Complete man-page coverage (372 public functions, strict gate).
  * CI: gcc + clang, ASan, UBSan, musl, coro-fctx, macOS, Windows/MSVC,
    5 TLS backends, sim-DST, and the nightly DST swarm -- all green.

