libxtc (0.8.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Preemption facility (native, inspired by CMU's Lightweight
    Preemptible Functions; see docs/M_PREEMPTION.md):
    - Phase 0: a per-worker CPU-time interval timer seam
      (xtc_preempt_arm/disarm; POSIX per-thread CPU-time timers,
      NOSYS elsewhere).
    - Phase 0.5: a per-thread async-signal-unsafe-region depth counter
      (__xtc_unsafe_enter/leave) bracketing the allocator, realizing
      libas-safe's discipline via a counter -- also hardens the fault
      handler against unwinding out of a corrupt malloc arena.
    - Phase 1 (SUPPORTED): cooperative-assisted preemption --
      xtc_exec_set_preempt(interval_ns) arms the timer per worker, and a
      tick makes xtc_yield_if_due callers yield, time-slicing a compute
      fiber with no manual budget.
    - Phase 2: the signal-context involuntary-yield infrastructure +
      safety gate (crit_depth + unsafe_depth) is in place; the resumable
      redirect declines for now (a portable whole-ucontext copy is
      unsound) and falls back to Phase 1, pending per-architecture
      mcontext surgery (Go's method).  Untrusted pure-CPU work uses
      xtc_osproc meanwhile.

